Package: extracttext
Title: Court Record Text Extraction, Deterministic and AI Compared
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Cheng", "Ren", role = "aut"),
    person("Tim", "Thomas", , "timthomas@berkeley.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Aaron", "Culich", , "aculich@berkeley.edu", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Extracts structured fields from United States court records, most
    often eviction and unlawful detainer filings, using rule-based and language
    model methods, then reports where the two disagree. Reads e-filed PDFs,
    scanned PDFs, and TIFFs; extracts party names, the defendant service
    address, and the plaintiff attorney block; and flags anything uncertain
    for human review. Wraps the Python extract_text engine through reticulate.
    Records processed with the default engines never leave the machine.
